5 · What We Learned

Confirmed: targeting works, and the alarm works on real hardware.
Surprise: quantum hardware only watches its own cable. Combining it with fiber monitoring catches 84% of small taps, against 56% for either alone.
Disproved: using a quantum computer for the planning.
Gap: two simultaneous cable cuts.
Next: real utility data, a pilot on EPB’s tested route, then water utilities.
Closing line: “A defensible quantum-security plan in seconds, for any network that can’t afford to guess.”

